    <!-- The notebook lying on the lawn: a page of kraft paper, its spiral, and the pitch
         drawn on it. The app's name says both halves — football and the note — and that is
         what the drawing shows, rather than one of the two.

         The icon's lawn is lighter than the tactical board's, which is a night green; here
         it has the launcher's dark background on one side and the paper on the other, and a
         night green would have merged into the former. The markings are white, as on a real
         pitch, and no longer in green ink: on that green they hold the 3:1 ratio a stroke
         must keep to stay legible, which is also why the paper is a light kraft and not a
         plain brown — any darker, it would bring the page closer to the background and leave
         the white to carry the icon on its own.

         The pitch stands upright, like the page, and takes up almost its full height: that
         is what leaves room for the penalty areas, and it is they, with the centre circle,
         that make it read as a pitch rather than a board. The corner arcs and the goal
         areas, for their part, would clog into a blot at forty-eight points and are left
         out.

         The rings are drawn short and thin: they name the object and nothing more, so the
         room they gave up at the top goes to the page, which is the part that carries the
         drawing. The page widened and rose by the same amount, and its bottom corners stop
         at the edge of the 66dp disc the launcher guarantees — that disc is what sets the
         size of everything here, rings included.

         Their brass is the one colour that holds at that size on both grounds the rings
         cross: the night green above the page, and the kraft below it. The lemon they were
         drawn in came close enough to the background's green to lose them once they went
         from four points thick to three. -->
    <path android:fillColor="#FFE7D3AE"
        android:pathData="M36.4,31.5 L71.6,31.5 Q76,31.5 76,35.9 L76,76.1 Q76,80.5 71.6,80.5 L36.4,80.5 Q32,80.5 32,76.1 L32,35.9 Q32,31.5 36.4,31.5 Z" />
    <path android:strokeColor="#FFE0A64A" android:strokeWidth="2.9" android:strokeLineCap="round"
